{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Walking in the garden.</b> The voice was walking, and we find elsewhere walking in connection with voice: 'the sound of the shofar going and growing very strong' (Exod. 19:19); 'her sound shall go like the serpent' ( Jer. 46:22)." "<b>At the wind of the day.</b> At the usual wind, for she had entered into it cunningly, and he would confess on his own; but not at an unusual wind, so that he would not have an opening to say: on account of the unusual wind I hid myself. Another interpretation: <b>at the wind of the day.</b> To cool themselves Adam and Eve were sitting, and when they heard the voice they fled from there and were found within the garden." "<b>At the wind of the day.</b> Rashi explained: a west wind, etc. And thus we hold, that the Shekhinah is in the west."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:40.289242886Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}